(param &box_size number (5))

(exclude ($ColorClass $KeyWithoutMarker $KeyInBox) "A reading with $ColorClass and $KeyInBox is defined only where each color's cells fit in one box with their key, and there they spread into one shape, so it gives the output of the same reading with $ShapeBySpread. Under $MarkerColor every color's cells fit in a box of the derived box-size, so with $BoxSizeFromShapes the two groupings agree everywhere, and the $ColorClass reading is the case. Under $KeyByNearest with the concept branch at every other point, only the derivation reads box-size, and it leaves the case undefined more often.")
(exclude ($ShapeBySpread $MarkerColor $BoxSizeFromShapes) "A reading with $ColorClass and $KeyInBox is defined only where each color's cells fit in one box with their key, and there they spread into one shape, so it gives the output of the same reading with $ShapeBySpread. Under $MarkerColor every color's cells fit in a box of the derived box-size, so with $BoxSizeFromShapes the two groupings agree everywhere, and the $ColorClass reading is the case. Under $KeyByNearest with the concept branch at every other point, only the derivation reads box-size, and it leaves the case undefined more often.")
(exclude ($ColorClass $KeyInBox $BoxSizeStored $StampAlignCenter) "A reading with $ColorClass and $KeyInBox is defined only where each color's cells fit in one box with their key, and there they spread into one shape, so it gives the output of the same reading with $ShapeBySpread. Under $MarkerColor every color's cells fit in a box of the derived box-size, so with $BoxSizeFromShapes the two groupings agree everywhere, and the $ColorClass reading is the case. Under $KeyByNearest with the concept branch at every other point, only the derivation reads box-size, and it leaves the case undefined more often.")
(exclude ($ColorClass $KeyInBox $BoxSizeStored $MarkerCleared) "A reading with $ColorClass and $KeyInBox is defined only where each color's cells fit in one box with their key, and there they spread into one shape, so it gives the output of the same reading with $ShapeBySpread. Under $MarkerColor every color's cells fit in a box of the derived box-size, so with $BoxSizeFromShapes the two groupings agree everywhere, and the $ColorClass reading is the case. Under $KeyByNearest with the concept branch at every other point, only the derivation reads box-size, and it leaves the case undefined more often.")
(exclude ($MarkerColor $KeyByNearest $BoxSizeFromShapes $StampFlush $MarkerKept) "A reading with $ColorClass and $KeyInBox is defined only where each color's cells fit in one box with their key, and there they spread into one shape, so it gives the output of the same reading with $ShapeBySpread. Under $MarkerColor every color's cells fit in a box of the derived box-size, so with $BoxSizeFromShapes the two groupings agree everywhere, and the $ColorClass reading is the case. Under $KeyByNearest with the concept branch at every other point, only the derivation reads box-size, and it leaves the case undefined more often.")

(alts $g
  (alt $ShapeBySpread
    (witness repeated-shape-color variant $ShapeBySpread
      (relaxed shapes)
      (separates "Two shapes far apart share color 3, keyed 4 and 6. The concept reads color 3 as one shape, which no key fits a box with, and is undefined; $ShapeBySpread splits color 3 into two shapes and swaps and stamps each.")
